{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>The owner of the pit.</b> The one responsible for the damage — even though the pit is not his, since he made it in the public domain — Scripture calls him its owner to hold him liable for its damages." "<b>He shall restore silver to its owner.</b> יָשִׁיב — to include anything worth silver, even bran (ibid. 7)." "<b>And the dead animal shall be his.</b> To the injured party — they appraise the carcass and he takes it in the payment, and the one who caused the damage pays him the balance of his loss (Bava Kamma 10)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {1 "the citation 'שם ז' (there 7) refers to the page in Bava Kamma cited in the next comment, i.e. Bava Kamma 7a/b"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:45.081440103Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}